< https://github.com/tacplus-dev/looper/issues/126#issuecomment-6798236906 [2026-11-11T14:17:30Z] checkpoint of #126 (a step) pushed to looper/looper-126:  8 files changed, 777 insertions(+), 10 deletions(-)
I've committed the fix for #126 (5e23082), but it isn't on main yet. The land has been queued with the manager since 11:22Z, with no verdict by 14:17Z, when my time ran out. The issue stays open: the manager lands it after this run, and the next run reads the verdict, writes the outcome comment and closes it.

**The fix, in `looper-scan`:**
- **Fallback:** when `cargo metadata` can't load a Cargo.toml that path-depends on generated crates, cargo-deny no longer gives up. It first runs on a copy of the tree with the gates' `generated/` placed at the tacplus.yaml `output-dir`.
- **Lock alone:** if that also fails, it checks every crate in `Cargo.lock` directly. This follows Jody's "point cargo-deny at the lock alone", and the summary says the check covered the lock only, and why.
- **Findings:** they still point at the source `Cargo.lock`.
- **Error message:** a cargo-deny that still can't run fails the run and gives cargo's own error. The old message was just `exited 1:`, because cargo-deny logs its errors as JSON and that text was dropped.

**What I checked:**
- **Tests:** four new cases in `tests/looper-build.test.sh` cover each path. They use a fake cargo-deny that fails the way `cargo metadata` does, and `looper-build: all passed`.
- **Gateway:** at cfe4600, without its generated crates, the real cargo-deny 0.20.2 now reports RUSTSEC-2026-0486 for rustix 1.1.4, plus five other RustSec advisories.
- **Other checks:** the docs check passes, and the trace check found no service handlers in this change.

**Not verified:**
- **Build job:** GitLab refused all three attempts with a 422. That's #118, an unescaped `+` in the gate set `docs+build`. Its fix is queued ahead of mine, so my land may hit the same 422 until #118 merges. If it does, the next run waits on #118 and lands again.
- **The `generated/` path:** I couldn't test it with the real cargo-deny, because tacplus doesn't run here. Only the fake covers it.
- **Gateway's original failure:** gateway's passing gates already keep the generated crates for the scan, so its failed scan most likely followed failed gates (the scan runs even then). I couldn't read the build logs to confirm.

I also added a follow-up to PROPOSALS.md: clippy fails the same way when the generated crates are missing. That failure shows as a problem in the verdict, so it isn't hidden. I updated README and STATE.md, posted all of this as a status comment on the issue, and checkpointed.
